{"title":"Nature: The Best Science Images of 2025","link":"https://kottke.org/25/12/nature-the-best-science-images-of-2025","date":1766002227000,"content":"\n        <p>Nature magazine has chosen <a href=\"https://www.nature.com/immersive/d41586-025-03935-3/index.html\">its favorite science images of the year</a>. I’ve featured a few of these on the site already — <a href=\"https://kottke.org/25/11/skydiving-the-sun\">Skydiving the Sun</a>, <a href=\"https://kottke.org/25/11/0047803-a-trio-of-photographers-i\">red sprites in the New Zealand sky</a> — so I picked a couple of other favorites to share:</p>\n\n<p><img src=\"/cdn-cgi/image/format=auto,fit=scale-down,width=1200,metadata=none/images/posts/01/img-48047-01.jpg\" srcset=\"/cdn-cgi/image/format=auto,fit=scale-down,width=500,metadata=none/images/posts/01/img-48047-01.jpg 500w, /cdn-cgi/image/format=auto,fit=scale-down,width=1200,metadata=none/images/posts/01/img-48047-01.jpg 1200w\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"1800\" height=\"1014\" alt=\"A pair of pleasingly circular clouds is illuminated by lava from the Villarrica volcano in Chile as night falls. The scene was captured by photographer Francisco Negroni, who takes regular trips to the volcano to monitor its activity.\" /></p>\n\n<p><img src=\"/cdn-cgi/image/format=auto,fit=scale-down,width=1200,metadata=none/images/posts/01/img-48047-02.jpg\" srcset=\"/cdn-cgi/image/format=auto,fit=scale-down,width=500,metadata=none/images/posts/01/img-48047-02.jpg 500w, /cdn-cgi/image/format=auto,fit=scale-down,width=1200,metadata=none/images/posts/01/img-48047-02.jpg 1200w\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"1800\" height=\"1013\" alt=\"It shows two male green frogs (Lithobates clamitans) fighting over territory. The picture was captured by Grayson Bell, a talented 13-year-old photographer who gave it the genius title ‘Baptism of the Unwilling Convert’.\" /></p>\n\n<p>The first was taken by <a href=\"https://www.francisconegroni.com/\">Francisco Negroni</a> of the Villarrica volcano in Chile (check out <a href=\"https://www.francisconegroni.com/\">his site</a> for more amazing photos of volcanos &amp; lightning). The second is by 13-year-old <a href=\"https://www.graysonbellphotography.com/\">Grayson Bell</a> of two green frogs fighting; Bell named his photo “Baptism of the Unwilling Convert”.</p>\n\n        \n\n         <p><strong>Tags:</strong> <a href=\"https://kottke.org/tag/best%20of\">best of</a> · <a href=\"https://kottke.org/tag/best%20of%202025\">best of 2025</a> · <a href=\"https://kottke.org/tag/photography\">photography</a> · <a href=\"https://kottke.org/tag/science\">science</a></p>\n\n         <p>💬 <a href=\"https://kottke.org/25/12/nature-the-best-science-images-of-2025\">Join the discussion on kottke.org</a> →</p>\n\n    ","author":"Jason Kottke","siteTitle":"Kottke","siteHash":"89a883271b4598f9b33ebe87be70d38557bcd266e68aee521a8f93622e0ab723","entryHash":"23be8611fedc751a33057b2035317585dc9642414fcdada57b3bb5da6c3b79e9","category":"Sites"}